Reduce to Rolle's Theorem. Let
$
  phi(x) = [g(x) - g(a)] [f(b) - f(a)] - [g(b) - g(a)][f(x) - f(a)],
$
so that
$
  phi'(x) = g'(x) [f(b) - f(a)] - f'(x) [g(b) - g(a)].
$
Then $phi(a) = 0 = phi(b)$, and Rolle's Theorem gives $c in (a, b)$ with $phi'(c) = 0$, which is the claimed identity. Taking $g$ to be the identity recovers the ordinary Mean Value Theorem.
